{
  "id": "27788_umetateru",
  "headword": "{埋|う}め{立|た}てる",
  "reading": "うめたてる",
  "romaji": "umetateru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to reclaim (land); to fill in",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to reclaim (land); to fill in",
      "explanation": "To fill in a body of water such as the sea, a river, or a marsh with earth or waste so as to create dry land."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27788_umetateru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{海|うみ}を{埋|う}め{立|た}てる。",
      "english": "To reclaim land from the sea.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27788_umetateru_ex2",
      "japanese": "その{空港|くうこう}は{海|うみ}を{埋|う}め{立|た}てて{造|つく}られた。",
      "english": "That airport was built on reclaimed land.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27788_umetateru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{湿地|しっち}を{埋|う}め{立|た}てて{住宅地|じゅうたくち}にする{計画|けいかく}が{進|すす}んでいる。",
      "english": "A plan to fill in the wetland and turn it into a residential area is moving forward.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive ichidan verb. Xを{埋|う}め{立|た}てる. Compound of {埋|う}める (to bury, to fill) + {立|た}てる. Specifically refers to filling in water to make new land.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {海|うみ}を{埋|う}め{立|た}てる: to reclaim land from the sea\n- {埋|う}め{立|た}て{地|ち}: reclaimed land\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {埋|う}める: to bury; to fill in — general; can fill a hole, a gap, or even a position\n- {干拓|かんたく}する: to reclaim by drainage — draining water away rather than filling with earth",
